WEBVTT

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>GUNDAM</i>

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>MOBILE SUIT</i>

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:17.870
<i>hoshi ga furishikiru penthouse de
In the penthouse that watches the stars fall...</i>

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:24.040
<i>sora no ORUGO-RU hitori kiiteta
I listened to Heaven's music box...</i>

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:30.460
<i>GARASU no RO-PU wo mekakushi de wataru
Walking, blindfolded, across a tight-rope of glass...</i>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:37.090
<i>minna sabishii SA-KASU no kodomo sa
Everyone is like, the lonely child of the circus.</i>

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:45.020
<i>hitori bocchi no kanashimi ni
The rope that creaks with the sadness of isolation...</i>

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.770
<i>kishinda tsuna ga kokoro de yureteru...
...is still locked deep in my heart...</i>

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:07.830
<i>yasashii me wo shita dareka ni aitai
I wish to meet the one who's eyes glow with warmth!</i>

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:25.980
<i>sasayaite kureyo soba ni iruyotte Silent Voice
Whisper to me that you'll always be there by my side, Silent Voice.</i>

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:38.280
I could hear the voices
of the Argama's crew again!

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.960
But it was an SOS!

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:43.820
That meant they were under enemy fire!

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.900
Beecha got carried away and
forced us to do a lot of extra work.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.550
That really got me, too!

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:53.080
On top of that, Ple is still
trembling over something...

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:58.470
I get it! Maybe she wilted
because Glemy was nearby?

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:04.460
AFTERNOON IN DUBLIN

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.560
Course confirmed!

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:15.890
Hold on!

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:18.020
- We're changing the schedule.
- Why is that?

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.980
We're done with repairs on the Mk. II.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.060
Good work!

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.710
Will it be all right?

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.500
Oh, about that thing.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.400
- Stand aside! I can't see in front of me!
- Sorry about that!

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.430
What is it, Elle?

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:32.410
We can only get this done
at quiet times like now.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:33.950
What do you want me to do?

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.370
Inventory check for clothing!

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.540
Divide it into stuff you need,
and stuff you don't!

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:38.860
Here!

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:41.420
So pretty! So much green!

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:44.230
This is a forest, right?
So this is a continent!

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.630
Earth is a pretty neat place!

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:49.920
This wasn't created naturally, though.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.180
But how else do you make a forest?

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:56.640
Silly girl. Humans planted the forests
of Europe through the previous centuries.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.240
Oh, so it's just like the colonies?

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.850
Right. There were too many people.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:05.220
If left alone, it would have
become like the Sahara desert.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.750
So that's why people migrated to space.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.450
Oh, Torres and Keithron, too.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.660
When you get a moment,
please go through your clothes, too!

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.700
You kids, too! Throw out this stuff!

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.900
Okay!

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.590
That HAS to go!

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:21.790
Captain, there's stuff
like this in here, too.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:24.290
B-But, that's not mine!

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:26.500
I didn't say it was yours, "Dad."

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.010
- What?!
- Captain! What course should I set?

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.610
- Change course to north-northwest!
- Roger!

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:49.400
So in the end, there was no one
who could handle that thing?

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:53.170
No. It seems there were no pilots who could synchronize with the psycommu.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.570
Why is that?

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.990
Because it forcibly controls
the consciousness.

00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:59.930
- I am fully aware of that!
- Yes, my lady!

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:04.120
The cargo will definitely reach Glemy?

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:07.810
Yes, my lady. Arius Moma, who went
ahead on the shuttle, will guarantee that.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.860
Arius Moma, eh.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.260
Rendezvous point with
the Sandra confirmed.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.270
All right.
Proceeding as planned.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:22.390
Master Arius, there's
something below the clouds.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.990
Something? An airplane?

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.690
It seems different.

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:26.960
T-The Argama?!

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.110
- What should we do?
- Attack!

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:33.360
Our mission isn't just mobile suit transport
but also guarding the cargo behind us!

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.990
The Bawoos don't have Base Jabbers!

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:36.710
We don't have time, either!

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.540
Why don't the boys help us?

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.250
They think this stuff is women's work.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.870
What is it, Astonaige?

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:50.290
I checked out the Qubeley. If you want
to win battles, you should be using Ple.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.320
She doesn't feel any pressure
from the psycomuu.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.010
But she still looks like a mere child.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.220
Captain, why did we change direction?

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.310
I thought we were heading
to the Karaba base in Norway!

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:02.020
- We turned west.
- Why is that!?

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.690
I have my reasons!

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.440
- Like what?
- I don't have time to--

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:08.000
Don't you want to see
your family, Captain?!

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.210
If we survive, I'll see them someday!

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.410
If we survive...?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.050
What's wrong, Judau?

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:21.930
Judau.

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:27.900
What's wrong, Ple?

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.250
Ple, come on, don't stop working.

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.840
- What's up?
- That's enough!

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:32.980
- Ple!
- Hey!

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.840
I guess we have to go
to Dublin after all.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.070
Dublin?

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.970
A city that used to be
part of Britain.

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:41.700
Let's have a doctor take a look at Ple.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:45.020
Ple! You think you can
just run off like that?!

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.730
Don't just get all pissed off
because you felt something!

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:50.120
I'm not wrong about this!

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:58.660
If we can pick up the Argama
as a souvenir along the way...

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:04.290
Master Arius, the cargo behind us
is now being guided by the Sandra!

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:08.600
D-Don't zoom in so much!

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:14.500
Just as planned, pilot the shuttle until
the last moment, then ram the ship!

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:16.020
I'm going out!

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:26.830
So, Captain, you're detouring
to Dublin to examine Ple?

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:28.740
That's just incidental.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.560
You know of the Beech
Mansion in Dublin, right?

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.120
You mean the one all the Earth
Federation higher-ups ran off to?

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.190
Captain!

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:36.940
Mobile suit silhouettes overhead!

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:38.820
- What?
- We don't know what they are.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.030
Hurry up and confirm them!

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:42.710
What's making you so cranky, Ple?

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.930
It's here!

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.000
- Ple!
- No!

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.790
Judau, I know you wish
I'd died instead of Leina!

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:55.400
I'd never think such a thing!

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.650
Lies!

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:02.190
What's that?

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:05.440
You've gotta help us fold them again!

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:07.070
Now's not the time for that!

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:09.690
- Ple?!
- She ran off?

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:14.250
Do you think it would make me happy
if you felt guilty and killed yourself.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:17.530
I care about you just as
much as Leina did, Judau!

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:18.460
Ouch!

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:19.490
Iino!

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:20.530
What are you trying to do?!

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:22.880
Enemy mobile suits are here!

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:25.330
You can't defeat the
enemy all by yourself!

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:26.890
Beecha! Get in the Core Top!

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:29.370
There's no mistake. They're Bawoos!

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:30.710
They're free-falling towards us!

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:32.250
Give orders to sortie!

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.880
Core Base is already moving!

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:35.290
- What?
- Ple?

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.050
Why is she going out?

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:39.560
Did she detect the enemy before we did?

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:45.470
I'll defeat the enemy,
even if I'm all alone!

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:46.550
You're not alone!

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.570
I'm the one piloting!

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:54.520
- Ple, stop trying to fight by yourself!
- It's reckless!

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:57.940
No! I'll fight by myself!
I don't care if I die!

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:00.380
No way! I don't wanna die!

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:06.840
Looks like some small fry came out!

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.640
If I die, then Judau will--

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.600
Don't die!

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:19.420
This one's mine!

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:21.310
Like I'm gonna let you!

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:30.100
Judau.

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:34.480
Fighting on your own won't
help me or anyone else.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:35.790
Judau!

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.420
Hmph, they don't even
have Base Jabbers.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:48.780
J-Just a bit more.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:50.510
Beecha! Behind you!

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:57.060
- Judau, where are you?
- I got it!

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:08.760
Their communication is very quick...!

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.950
What are you?!

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:18.750
If we're fighting the small fry,
the Argama will escape!

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:26.030
- Did he run away?!
- He's still nearby!

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.580
Where is he?

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.680
All right, dive into it now!

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:34.040
They're ramming us
with the shuttle!

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:35.080
That's impossible!

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.580
Captain, I think they don't
have a lot of control over it.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.580
We should shift our position!

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:40.940
- Do it, don't say it!
- Roger!

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.360
I-I can't see anything!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:52.470
Beecha! Increase your altitude!
Leave that area to Judau and Ple!

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:53.820
Roger!

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:58.040
Where is the Argama...?

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:01.710
Is it them? Where's the shuttle?

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:13.380
He escaped to a lower
altitude just for us.

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:16.180
Don't follow them too far down!

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:19.720
Yeah, Judau.

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:24.940
Ple, are you talking to Judau?

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.070
This one's mine!

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:33.900
It's over--

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:39.330
Tetoas, out of the way!

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:47.400
A flash! Two o'clock!

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:48.710
It's not falling yet!

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.570
Evade it! Quickly!

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.310
Good girl, Ple!
The Argama was saved!

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:12.150
Hey! Where are you guys? Is it over?

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:13.860
What?

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:21.950
W-What was that?

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:28.330
They even shot down the shuttle,
using only small craft.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.290
Damn the Argama.

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:58.030
Can't you tell from my uniform
that I'm not suspicious!

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:02.490
And who might you be?
Please state your full name and rank.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:24.000
Looks like they don't have
enough tree branches!

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.880
Hey, are you listening?

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:27.100
Huh?

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.900
- They found us!
- Found us, found us!

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:34.380
And what are you guys doing?

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:36.360
I said we can go shopping later!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:39.470
I was hoping to get out of here
without pissing you off, but whatever.

00:12:39.470 --> 00:12:41.870
Hold up!

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:45.660
It must be nice to be so simple-minded.

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:54.780
This thing is a mess!

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:55.990
How did you get this one?

00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:58.370
This city doesn't have
any decent rental cars!

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:00.870
Why didn't the Argama enter the port?

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:03.700
If it entered the port, it'd be obvious
what the Argama's doing, right?

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:07.290
If we headed straight to Norway, I'm sure
Karaba would've been waiting, too.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.640
I heard that there's a really
good doctor in this city.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:11.420
There's nothing wrong with me!

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:13.460
You get sick pretty easy though, right?

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:15.630
That's the reason they let you leave.

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:17.300
- But...
- No buts.

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:18.950
Hey, hey, isn't that it?

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:20.890
The house that Captain Bright went to!

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:22.470
Was it somewhere around here?

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:24.480
Don't they call it Beech Mansion?

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:27.140
You know, where all the Federation
Forces higher-ups went.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:30.250
So the Federation adults are there?

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:32.790
Judau! Where are you going?!

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.240
I'll catch up with you.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.490
Ple, be good and go see the doctor.

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:37.910
What should we do?

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:39.740
We have to go get our
shopping done, anyway.

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:40.490
All right!

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:41.550
Judau!

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:44.380
Make sure to do what they tell you!

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:53.760
Even in times like these,

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:56.720
I can't imagine why anyone would
eat synthetic meat.

00:13:56.720 --> 00:13:59.820
Well, it's not good
to gain too much weight.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:02.680
And I'm a smoker, too, Admiral.

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:03.600
Oh, dear.

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:04.600
Your Excellency.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:06.520
I have brought you a guest.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:07.270
A guest?

00:14:07.270 --> 00:14:08.200
Excuse me.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.520
We're in the middle of a meal!

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:13.630
I am Bright Noa, captain of the Argama.

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:14.940
The Argama?!

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:16.570
Why didn't you say that first?!

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:18.530
I-I am terribly sorry!

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:22.200
It seems that it's inconvenient for me
to be the captain of the Argama.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.470
No... such a thing...

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:27.080
...is true, Captain Bright.

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:30.750
You oppose our peace
policies, don't you?

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:36.480
Are you telling me that giving Side 3
to Haman Karn is a peace policy?!

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:51.230
Haman says that's her condition
for signing a ceasefire treaty.

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:54.290
If the war ends, there'll
be peace. Am I wrong?

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:58.110
Side 3 is where Zeon was born.

00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:01.820
Doing such a thing will only
add fuel to the fire of Neo Zeon!

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:04.160
Don't you understand what that means?

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:07.250
Haman will settle down
after she gets Side 3.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:10.770
Doesn't the AEUG want to make
more money from this war?

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:15.740
All the rumors say the AEUG is in league
with Anaheim Electronics on the moon.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:19.350
The Argama will withdraw to Norway,
and be decommissioned.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:22.180
So how about it? Want to
sit and drink with us?

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:24.550
We have fresh vegetables, too!

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:32.690
Do you understand the meaning
of what you're saying?!

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:35.770
Career soldiers can be
so annoyingly stubborn.

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:39.390
And what do you know,
lounging around on Earth?!

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:40.250
Judau?

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.360
Who are you?

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:44.920
Dammit! Don't you guys know
what Haman's really like?

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:46.660
S-Someone!

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:50.080
Do you know how much
we've suffered in these battles?

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:51.740
Leina even died!

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:54.670
And yet, you think we
WANT to keep fighting?

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:56.000
S-Stop it!

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:01.300
Because you people sit here
doing NOTHING, the world's going to hell!

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:02.180
Judau, stop it!

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:03.260
But these guys--

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:04.530
Freeze!

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:08.890
Is this one of your subordinates, Bright?

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:11.440
What a belligerent child.

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:13.870
I'm here to pick up the dirty laundry.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:16.820
- Thank you for your work.
- Sure.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:22.730
Surgery Department 1,
Dr. Elizabeth, call on line 12.

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:28.750
Surgery Department 1,
Dr. Elizabeth, call on line 12.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:32.120
Go see your friend now.

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:33.600
Okay!

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:38.930
Don't run down the hallway!

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:40.350
What?

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.180
That girl smells familiar.

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:49.100
What is that smell?

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:51.020
The Argama?

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:52.650
I-It can't be.

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:58.190
How was it?

00:16:58.190 --> 00:17:01.490
They don't trust us only with
Captain Bright's written request.

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:03.110
Maybe they're quacks?

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:04.820
There's nothing wrong with me!

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:07.070
Mondo! Iino! Come help me!

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:09.260
Sure thing!

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:10.540
Wait!

00:17:10.540 --> 00:17:11.990
Hey, where's Judau?

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:13.850
He's not here yet!

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:16.960
Not yet? Maybe he went
back to the Argama.

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:17.850
Maybe so.

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:19.540
I wonder what happened?

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.510
This city seems so cluttered,
and I can't figure it out.

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:25.130
You know, why don't you help
out at least a little bit?

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:26.800
- Here!
- Thanks!

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:28.970
It'll be okay if Beecha
works harder!

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:31.570
You know, Ple...

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:39.910
Master Glemy, I appreciate your granting my
request so soon after I took up this new post.

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:43.610
Oh no, it's a reward for bringing
something very precious.

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:45.070
- Do as you wish.
- Yes, sir!

00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:46.150
Course confirmed!

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:49.300
All right! Go, Arius!

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:58.670
There can be no doubt
the Argama landed in Dublin.

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:00.130
Any new information?

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:01.930
It seems they didn't enter the port.

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:05.270
But those Earth Federation
people are in Dublin!

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.260
Hey, let us out of here!

00:18:12.260 --> 00:18:15.140
Come on, locking us up
doesn't accomplish anything!

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:16.270
Hey!

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:18.020
Come on! Dammit!

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:20.020
Judau, it's useless.

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:23.980
Are they planning to keep us here
until we shrivel up and die?

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:25.530
Perhaps.

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:29.320
I'm sure those guys don't intend
to stick around here forever.

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:34.030
If we don't get a move on, they'll
decommission the Argama right here.

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:35.570
What's that?!

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:37.720
Artillery fire? An air strike?!

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:43.630
Now, spread out your attacks
as much as possible.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:46.400
- That will lure them out more effectively.
- Roger.

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:02.810
- You saw a mobile suit?
- I saw one unit!

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:05.290
You mean two units!
Worry about carrying the luggage later!

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:07.980
But Judau is still near the city!

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:10.420
You didn't bring
Captain Bright with you?

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.620
Hurry up!

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:15.280
Move faster!

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:19.350
If they attack us here,
we're done for! Hey!

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:33.360
Damn you, Argama! If you're
not in the port, then where?!

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:38.960
- Quickly, begin first aid!
- Okay!

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:40.850
It's not that bad a wound!

00:19:40.850 --> 00:19:43.600
Miss Fa, I'm sorry you
have to do this too!

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:45.440
It's all right. I begged them
to give me this job.

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:47.040
Out of the way!

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.330
Hey, let us out!

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:53.090
Is anyone out there?! Open up!

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:55.780
Are you going to leave us here to die?!

00:19:56.070 --> 00:19:57.990
If we can't do anything...

00:19:57.990 --> 00:19:59.620
Someone!

00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:02.690
Dammit! Open up!

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:07.310
Someone... there are... people in here!

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:12.610
That voice... I know it!

00:20:19.340 --> 00:20:22.850
Double Zeta, stand by a little longer,
in case Judau comes back!

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:25.480
Beecha, lure the enemy
toward the sea or the mountains!

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:27.500
You don't have to tell me that!

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:34.380
- It's those guys from earlier!
- Two enemy units!

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:39.130
Even though Dublin isn't a military base,
those mobile suits...!

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:40.620
Glad you could make it out!

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:42.300
Now, where's the Argama?!

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:51.010
M-My breath...

00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:52.610
C-Captain!

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:55.840
Judau... the smoke's
already flooding the basement!

00:20:55.840 --> 00:20:57.030
Is anyone in there?

00:20:57.030 --> 00:20:59.450
If anyone is down there,
please answer me!

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:01.440
W-We're down here!

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:03.930
We can't get out!
Can you help us?

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:08.370
I-I'm not sure. But I'll try!
Please stand back!

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:10.520
Is this all right?

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:13.240
Unfortunately, I don't--

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:19.720
I know that voice... who is it?

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:30.060
- J-Judau.
- Y-Yeah.

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:35.070
Wait...

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:39.740
Oh, it really is you!
Captain! And Judau!

00:21:39.740 --> 00:21:42.030
Captain?

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.890
Is that you, Fa Yuiry?

00:21:43.890 --> 00:21:45.850
Yes, yes!

00:21:45.850 --> 00:21:47.140
It's me, Fa Yuiry!

00:21:47.140 --> 00:21:50.330
Please hurry! This entire
building looks dangerous now!

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:51.520
Thank you!

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:52.820
Judau, get up!

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:54.860
I'm fine. Captain, go on ahead!

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:56.430
Thank you!

00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:57.820
Fa...

00:21:57.820 --> 00:22:00.160
Fa Yuiry, the one who was with Kamille.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:02.260
- Judau!
- Yeah!

00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:07.420
- Let's go!
- All right!

00:22:11.370 --> 00:22:13.380
Is the Argama nearby?

00:22:13.380 --> 00:22:15.710
It's on the other side of the hill.
Can you get us there?

00:22:15.710 --> 00:22:17.110
Of course.

00:22:21.880 --> 00:22:24.860
Miss Fa, what are you
doing in a city like this?

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:28.870
I was going to ask you that! Why Dublin?

00:22:29.220 --> 00:22:33.540
I came to shed tears after
being smothered in smoke.

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:50.820
<i>ikuyaku ikuman ikuoku no hoshi yo
Hundreds upon thousands upon millions of stars...</i>

00:22:50.820 --> 00:22:56.950
<i>naze hikaru dake nano ka kataru chikara no shiwase
...why do you just sit there and twinkle? Show me the power that lets me connect!</i>

00:22:56.950 --> 00:23:08.050
<i>Ima nara ore demo furikaerasu ni tobitatsu kokoro
For now, even I've got a mind that wanders without reminiscing past regrets!</i>

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:13.930
<i>Hoshi no kazu dake inochi wo takuwareba
If lives are really stored in the form of stars...</i>

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:19.940
<i>ginga no mure no hikari wo kaete misero
...show me how to change the light and move galaxies...</i>

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:29.650
<i>kono te ga tsukamu inochi no omosa ni naru
The weight of life itself, will be held in my hands!</i>

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:35.530
<i>mada meinai yo sora no michishirude wa
Space's guidepost is still not within my sights...</i>

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:41.620
<i>kono te ni saware hikari isenmanen
Let the light of 10 million years touch this hand!</i>

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:48.710
While they were demanding that
we decommission the Argama...

00:23:48.710 --> 00:23:51.580
Fa came to tell us that
Kamille had gone missing.

00:23:51.580 --> 00:23:53.500
We couldn't just leave him alone.

00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:57.880
While we were out searching,
Arius attacked us again.

00:23:57.880 --> 00:24:01.840
Ple did her best, but it's hard for her to
fight in a machine that doesn't suit her.

00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:04.100
Ple! Don't die!

00:24:04.100 --> 00:24:07.800
Next time on Gundam ZZ:
"Kamille's Voice."

00:24:05.810 --> 00:24:08.930
Next Time

00:24:05.810 --> 00:24:08.930
KAMILLE'S VOICE

00:24:08.600 --> 00:24:11.310
Kamille's alive?
But of course!
